  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: \n\nIsolated showers and thunderstorms are expected across portions of\nnortheastern Elko County this afternoon. Otherwise dry and storm-\nfree across the CWA. South to southwest winds of 10 to 20 mph\ngusting 20 to 35 mph are expected in most areas this afternoon as\ntrough energy approaches from the Pacific NW. The approaching\nsystem will also result in a few degrees of cooling both today and\nagain on Wednesday. \n\nAn upper level area of low pressure will make landfall along the\ncoast of the Pacific Northwest Thursday. This cyclone aloft will\nmeander around the coast of the Pacific Northwest Friday into the\nupcoming weekend. Meanwhile, a tropical cyclone will be located in\nthe Eastern Pacific, just west of the Baja Peninsula this weekend.\nThere are indications that these two storm systems may interact\nwith each other, drawing atmospheric moisture northward. At this\ntime, low forecast confidence exists in this scenario. Timing,\ncoverage, and extent of any precipitation late this weekend into\nearly next week will need to be further refined in the upcoming \nfew days. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence in the\npossibility of a few strong thunderstorms in Eastern Elko County \nthis afternoon. High forecast confidence regarding a cooling \ntrend today and Wednesday. Low forecast confidence in periods of \nrain this weekend into early next week.",
